From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clemens Backes <clemensb@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:27:59 +0200
Subject: [wasm] Match source URL when reusing cached Scripts in WasmEngine

WasmEngine::GetOrCreateScript previously cached a single weak Script per
(Isolate*, NativeModule*) without checking whether the caller's
source_url matched the existing Script::name(). When two contexts in the
same Isolate compiled identical Wasm wire bytes with different source
URLs, the second compilation reused the first compilation's Script and
exposed its source URL in exception stack traces.

Allow IsolateInfo::scripts to hold multiple WeakScriptHandles per
NativeModule* and only reuse an existing Script in GetOrCreateScript if
its source URL matches the requested source_url.

TAG=agy
R=jkummerow@chromium.org

Bug: 564190098
Change-Id: Iae1aabdfc936c46437e302a7a5c59e892a23f525
